# Keep the build context lean: skip host node_modules (npm ci rebuilds them
# in the client stage), any stale local dist (Docker stage produces a fresh
# one), the .git history, local SQLite DBs, secrets, IDE state, and pytest
# / mypy caches. Otherwise the 88MB+ host modules dir lands in every COPY,
# busts the Docker cache, and risks a stale dist shadowing the fresh build.
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache

client/dist
client/.vite
client/*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.gitignore
.github

instance/*.db
instance/*.db-*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

.env
.env.local
client/.env.local
permissions.env

.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
*.swp
*.log

# Tests + dev-only configs don't need to be in the image.
tests/
docs/
*.md
